{% extends "_base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}BugOut Index — {{ snapshot.bugout_index }} · {{ snapshot.interpretation.band }}{% endblock %}
{% block body %}

<section class="hero">
  <div>{{ gauge|safe }}</div>
  <div>
    <div class="label">Week of {{ snapshot.publication_date }}</div>
    <h2>{{ snapshot.interpretation.band }}</h2>
    <div class="sub">{{ snapshot.interpretation.risk }}. A directional reading of six published statistics against fixed endpoints, as one 0–100 score. Higher means less stress. Not a forecast, and not an instruction to bug out.</div>
    <span class="band {{ snapshot.interpretation.band_key }}">{{ snapshot.interpretation.band }}</span>
    <div class="delta">
      {% if boi_delta is not none %}
        Week-over-week: <strong>{{ "%+.2f"|format(boi_delta) }}</strong> points
      {% else %}
        Week-over-week: <strong>first recorded week</strong>
      {% endif %}
      · {{ history_count }} week(s) of history
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% if week_note %}
<section class="week-note" aria-label="What changed this week">
  <h3>This week</h3>
  {% for sentence in week_note %}
  <p{% if loop.last %} class="disclaimer"{% endif %}>{{ sentence }}</p>
  {% endfor %}
</section>
{% endif %}

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>Core metrics</h3>
  <span class="hint">Each tile shows the raw value, how old that reading is, the normalized 0–100 score, and the raw weight (weights sum to 0.72; see Methodology for shares of the finished index).</span>
</div>
<p class="rev-callout">
  Headline labor numbers move after release. See how much the last 24 months of payrolls
  have been revised on the <a href="./revisions.html">data revisions tracker</a>.
</p>
<div class="grid metrics">
  {% for m in metrics %}
  <div class="tile{% if m.stale %} stale{% endif %}">
    <div class="k">{{ m.label }}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ m.raw|fmt(m.unit) }}</div>
    {{ m.sparkline|safe }}
    <div class="norm-bar"><span style="width: {{ m.normalized or 0 }}%"></span></div>
    <div class="meta">
      <span>Normalized {{ (m.normalized if m.normalized is not none else '—') }} / 100</span>
      <span>Raw weight {{ m.weight_pct }}%</span>
    </div>
    <div class="meta">
      <span><a href="{{ m.source_url }}">{{ m.source }}</a></span>
    </div>
    <div class="age">{{ m.age_text }}{% if m.stale %} <span class="badge-stale">Stale</span>{% endif %}</div>
    {% if m.diagnostics and not m.diagnostics.index_input %}
    <div class="age">Candidate {{ m.diagnostics.candidate_incident_rate }} per 100k for {{ m.diagnostics.candidate_month }} (population-weighted {{ m.diagnostics.population_weighted_incident_rate }}). Not an index input; the published crime figure stays {{ m.raw }}.</div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>Markets — weekly close</h3>
  <span class="hint">Spot gold &amp; silver (USD/oz) from <a href="https://gold-api.com">gold-api.com</a>; Broad US Dollar Index from <a href="https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/DTWEXBGS">FRED (DTWEXBGS)</a>.</span>
</div>
<div class="grid markets">
  {% for mk in markets %}
  <div class="tile">
    <div class="k">{{ mk.label }}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ mk.value|fmt(mk.unit) }}</div>
    {{ mk.sparkline|safe }}
    <div class="meta">
      <span>Week close</span>
      <span>
        {% if mk.delta is not none %}
          <span class="{{ 'delta-up' if mk.delta >= 0 else 'delta-down' }}">
            {{ "%+.2f"|format(mk.delta) }}% WoW
          </span>
        {% else %}
          —
        {% endif %}
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>Short-term pulse</h3>
  <span class="hint">Faster-moving indicators outside the BugOut Index. Each tile shows the observation date and age. Source: <a href="https://fred.stlouisfed.org">FRED</a>.</span>
</div>
<div class="grid pulse">
  {% for p in pulse %}
  <div class="tile{% if p.stale %} stale{% endif %}">
    <div class="k">{{ p.label }}{% if p.stale %} <span class="badge-stale">Stale</span>{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ p.value|fmt(p.unit) }}</div>
    {{ p.sparkline|safe }}
    <div class="meta">
      <span><a href="https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/{{ p.source_id }}">{{ p.source_id }}</a></span>
    </div>
    <div class="age">{{ p.age_text }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>Labor utilization — shadow series</h3>
  <span class="hint">Not in the BugOut Index. No weight. Prime-age (25–54) employment-population ratio and labor-force participation, monthly and seasonally adjusted, from BLS via FRED.</span>
</div>
<p class="rev-callout">
  These readings are companions only. They are not in the BugOut Index and they have no weight.
  Replacing headline unemployment still requires a backtest.
  {% if labor_reused_from %}
  This week’s fetch failed; values are carried forward from the {{ labor_reused_from }} publish. The dates below are the FRED observation dates.
  {% endif %}
</p>
<div class="grid labor">
  {% for tile in labor_tiles %}
  <div class="tile{% if tile.stale %} stale{% endif %}">
    <div class="k">{{ tile.label }}{% if tile.stale %} <span class="badge-stale">Stale</span>{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ tile.value|fmt(tile.unit, 1) }}</div>
    <div class="meta">
      <span><a href="{{ tile.source_url }}">FRED {{ tile.source_id }}</a></span>
      <span>not in the BugOut Index</span>
    </div>
    <div class="age">{{ tile.age_text }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% if labor_chart %}
<div class="chart-card">{{ labor_chart|safe }}</div>
<p class="chart-caption">Each point is a FRED observation month, not a BugOut Index publication week. Not in the BugOut Index.</p>
{% endif %}

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>Food prices — shadow series</h3>
  <span class="hint">Not in the BugOut Index. No weight. Food CPI, 12-month percent change, not seasonally adjusted, from BLS via FRED.</span>
</div>
<p class="rev-callout">
  This reading is a companion only. It is not in the BugOut Index and it has no weight.
  The figure is the public 12-month change in food prices
  (<a href="https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/CPIUFDNS">FRED CPIUFDNS</a>,
  BLS <a href="https://data.bls.gov/timeseries/CUUR0000SAF1?output_view=pct_12mths">CUUR0000SAF1</a>),
  rounded to one decimal the way BLS prints that table. It is not a score.
  {% if food_reused_from %}
  This week’s fetch failed; the value is carried forward from the {{ food_reused_from }} publish. The date below is the FRED observation date.
  {% endif %}
</p>
<div class="grid food">
  {% for tile in food_tiles %}
  <div class="tile{% if tile.stale %} stale{% endif %}">
    <div class="k">{{ tile.label }}{% if tile.stale %} <span class="badge-stale">Stale</span>{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ tile.value|fmt(tile.unit, 1) }}</div>
    <div class="meta">
      <span><a href="{{ tile.source_url }}">FRED {{ tile.source_id }}</a></span>
      <span>not in the BugOut Index</span>
    </div>
    <div class="age">{{ tile.age_text }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% if food_chart %}
<div class="chart-card">{{ food_chart|safe }}</div>
<p class="chart-caption">Each point is a FRED observation month, not a BugOut Index publication week. Not in the BugOut Index.</p>
{% endif %}

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>U.S. regional shelter companions</h3>
  <span class="hint">Not in the BugOut Index. No weight. Northeast New York City, Southeast Nashville–Davidson, South Austin/Travis County, Midwest Ramsey County, Southwest Denver, West San Francisco. None is a U.S. total. HUD AHAR remains the annual national homelessness input.</span>
</div>

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>Northeast — NYC DHS shelter census</h3>
  <span class="hint">Not in the BugOut Index. No weight. New York City only — not a U.S. total. Daily count of individuals in the NYC Department of Homeless Services shelter system. HUD AHAR remains the annual national homelessness input.</span>
</div>
<p class="rev-callout">
  This reading is a companion only. It is not in the BugOut Index and it has no weight.
  It is a New York City headcount from
  <a href="https://data.cityofnewyork.us/Social-Services/DHS-Daily-Report/k46n-sa2m">NYC Open Data {{ nyc_dataset_id }}</a>
  (field <code>total_individuals_in_shelter</code>), not a national rate and not a substitute for the HUD AHAR homelessness input.
  {% if nyc_reused_from %}
  This week’s fetch failed; the value is carried forward from the {{ nyc_reused_from }} publish. The date below is the DHS census date.
  {% endif %}
</p>
<div class="grid nyc">
  {% for tile in nyc_tiles %}
  <div class="tile{% if tile.stale %} stale{% endif %}">
    <div class="k">{{ tile.label }}{% if tile.stale %} <span class="badge-stale">Stale</span>{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ tile.value|fmt(tile.unit, 0) }}</div>
    <div class="meta">
      <span><a href="{{ tile.source_url }}">NYC Open Data {{ tile.dataset_id }}</a></span>
      <span>NYC only · not in the BugOut Index</span>
    </div>
    <div class="age">{{ tile.age_text }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% if nyc_chart %}
<div class="chart-card">{{ nyc_chart|safe }}</div>
<p class="chart-caption">Each point is a DHS census date, not a BugOut Index publication week. New York City only. Not in the BugOut Index.</p>
{% endif %}

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>Southeast — Nashville–Davidson shelter checklist</h3>
  <span class="hint">Not in the BugOut Index. No weight. Nashville–Davidson only — not a U.S. total. Monthly HMIS count of people who experienced homelessness. Not a one-night shelter census. HUD AHAR remains the annual national homelessness input.</span>
</div>
<p class="rev-callout">
  This reading is a companion only. It is not in the BugOut Index and it has no weight.
  It is copied from the Metro Nashville Office of Homeless Services
  <a href="https://www.nashville.gov/departments/office-homeless-services/homeless-management-information-system/monthly-data-reports">HMIS monthly data reports</a>.
  The latest row is people who experienced homelessness in Nashville during that month.
  Nashville Rescue Mission figures on the same PDF are separate and are not added.
  A person updates <code>runtime/data/shelter_region_shadow.csv</code>. The weekly job does not download the PDF.
  {% if region_reused_from %}
  This week’s checklist read failed; the value is carried forward from the {{ region_reused_from }} publish. The date below is the month in the checklist.
  {% endif %}
</p>
<div class="grid nyc">
  {% for tile in nashville_tiles %}
  <div class="tile">
    <div class="k">{{ tile.label }}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ tile.value|fmt(tile.unit, 0) }}</div>
    <div class="meta">
      <span><a href="{{ tile.source_url }}">Nashville HMIS monthly report</a></span>
      <span>Nashville–Davidson only · not in the BugOut Index</span>
    </div>
    <div class="age">{{ tile.question }}{% if tile.period %} · {{ tile.period }}{% endif %} · {{ tile.age_text }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% if nashville_chart %}
<div class="chart-card">{{ nashville_chart|safe }}</div>
<p class="chart-caption">Each point is a month from the checklist, not a BugOut Index publication week. Nashville–Davidson only. Not in the BugOut Index.</p>
{% endif %}

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>South — Austin/Travis County shelter checklist</h3>
  <span class="hint">Not in the BugOut Index. No weight. Austin/Travis County only — not a U.S. total. The public dashboard lags the month it names. HUD AHAR remains the annual national homelessness input.</span>
</div>
<p class="rev-callout">
  This reading is a companion only. It is not in the BugOut Index and it has no weight.
  It is the ECHO
  <a href="https://echoatx.github.io/hrs-dashboard-site/">Homelessness Response System dashboard</a>
  card for people engaged in the past six months and likely experiencing sheltered homelessness.
  The June 2025 dashboard was published September 10, 2025, with a data-effective date of July 1, 2025.
  That publication lag stays on the tile. A person updates the checklist. The weekly job does not scrape the dashboard.
</p>
<div class="grid nyc">
  {% for tile in austin_tiles %}
  <div class="tile">
    <div class="k">{{ tile.label }}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ tile.value|fmt(tile.unit, 0) }}</div>
    <div class="meta">
      <span><a href="{{ tile.source_url }}">ECHO HRS dashboard</a></span>
      <span>Austin/Travis County only · not in the BugOut Index</span>
    </div>
    <div class="age">{{ tile.question }}{% if tile.period %} · {{ tile.period }}{% endif %} · {{ tile.age_text }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>Midwest — Ramsey County shelter census</h3>
  <span class="hint">Not in the BugOut Index. No weight. Ramsey County, Minnesota only — not a U.S. total. Monthly sum of people in emergency shelters across published household types. HUD AHAR remains the annual national homelessness input.</span>
</div>
<p class="rev-callout">
  This reading is a companion only. It is not in the BugOut Index and it has no weight.
  It is a Ramsey County headcount from
  <a href="https://data.ramseycountymn.gov/dataset/Emergency-shelter-population-and-utilization/9mck-bcqu">Ramsey County open data {{ ramsey_dataset_id }}</a>
  (field <code>population_enrollees</code>, summed across household types), not a national rate and not a substitute for the HUD AHAR homelessness input.
  {% if ramsey_reused_from %}
  This week’s fetch failed; the value is carried forward from the {{ ramsey_reused_from }} publish. The date below is the county month stamp.
  {% endif %}
</p>
<div class="grid nyc">
  {% for tile in ramsey_tiles %}
  <div class="tile{% if tile.stale %} stale{% endif %}">
    <div class="k">{{ tile.label }}{% if tile.stale %} <span class="badge-stale">Stale</span>{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ tile.value|fmt(tile.unit, 0) }}</div>
    <div class="meta">
      <span><a href="{{ tile.source_url }}">Ramsey County {{ tile.dataset_id }}</a></span>
      <span>Ramsey County only · not in the BugOut Index</span>
    </div>
    <div class="age">{{ tile.age_text }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% if ramsey_chart %}
<div class="chart-card">{{ ramsey_chart|safe }}</div>
<p class="chart-caption">Each point is a county month, not a BugOut Index publication week. Ramsey County only. Not in the BugOut Index.</p>
{% endif %}

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>Southwest — Denver shelter checklist</h3>
  <span class="hint">Not in the BugOut Index. No weight. Denver only — not a U.S. total. This is an occupancy rate for a seven-shelter pilot, not a headcount. HUD AHAR remains the annual national homelessness input.</span>
</div>
<p class="rev-callout">
  This reading is a companion only. It is not in the BugOut Index and it has no weight.
  It is the occupancy rate Denver HOST published for its performance-based contracting pilot
  (seven shelters, 769 units) in the
  <a href="https://www.denvergov.org/Government/Agencies-Departments-Offices/Agencies-Departments-Offices-Directory/Department-of-Housing-Stability/News/HOST-Announces-Strong-Early-Results-from-Performance-Based-Contracting-Pilot">August 4, 2026 results</a>.
  The monthly citywide view is the
  <a href="https://www.denvergov.org/Government/Agencies-Departments-Offices/Agencies-Departments-Offices-Directory/Mayors-Office/Programs-and-Initiatives/Homelessness-Initiative/All-In-Mile-High-Dashboard">All In Mile High dashboard</a>.
  A person copies the next cited figure into the checklist. The weekly job does not scrape that dashboard.
</p>
<div class="grid nyc">
  {% for tile in denver_tiles %}
  <div class="tile">
    <div class="k">{{ tile.label }}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ tile.value|fmt(tile.unit, 0) }}</div>
    <div class="meta">
      <span><a href="{{ tile.source_url }}">Denver HOST</a></span>
      <span>Denver only · occupancy rate · not in the BugOut Index</span>
    </div>
    <div class="age">{{ tile.question }}{% if tile.period %} · {{ tile.period }}{% endif %} · {{ tile.age_text }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>West — San Francisco shelter occupancy</h3>
  <span class="hint">Not in the BugOut Index. No weight. San Francisco only — not a U.S. total. This is an occupancy rate, not a headcount. HUD AHAR remains the annual national homelessness input.</span>
</div>
<p class="rev-callout">
  This reading is a companion only. It is not in the BugOut Index and it has no weight.
  It is the monthly average occupancy rate of year-round temporary shelter and crisis intervention programs from
  <a href="https://data.sf.gov/City-Management-and-Ethics/Scorecard-Measures/kc49-udxn">DataSF {{ sf_dataset_id }}</a>
  measure <code>279</code>. The source stores a ratio; this tile shows percent. It is not a person count and not a substitute for the HUD AHAR homelessness input.
  {% if sf_reused_from %}
  This week’s fetch failed; the value is carried forward from the {{ sf_reused_from }} publish. The date below is the scorecard month.
  {% endif %}
</p>
<div class="grid nyc">
  {% for tile in sf_tiles %}
  <div class="tile{% if tile.stale %} stale{% endif %}">
    <div class="k">{{ tile.label }}{% if tile.stale %} <span class="badge-stale">Stale</span>{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ tile.value|fmt(tile.unit, 1) }}</div>
    <div class="meta">
      <span><a href="{{ tile.source_url }}">DataSF {{ tile.dataset_id }}</a></span>
      <span>San Francisco only · occupancy rate · not in the BugOut Index</span>
    </div>
    <div class="age">{{ tile.age_text }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% if sf_chart %}
<div class="chart-card">{{ sf_chart|safe }}</div>
<p class="chart-caption">Each point is a scorecard month, not a BugOut Index publication week. San Francisco only. Not a headcount. Not in the BugOut Index.</p>
{% endif %}


<div class="section-title">
  <h3>Pew public trust — shadow series</h3>
  <span class="hint">Not in the BugOut Index. No weight. Share who trust the government in Washington to do what is right just about always or most of the time. Irregular. Not the Edelman figure in the score.</span>
</div>
<p class="rev-callout">
  This reading is a companion only. It is not in the BugOut Index and it has no weight.
  The levels are not interchangeable with the Edelman Trust Barometer US Government input
  (survey year 2025, value 41). The weekly job reads a short excerpt from the checklist.
  It does not download Pew’s full series.
  {% if pew_reused_from %}
  This week’s checklist read failed; the value is carried forward from the {{ pew_reused_from }} publish. The date below is the survey date in the checklist.
  {% endif %}
</p>
<div class="grid pew">
  {% for tile in pew_tiles %}
  <div class="tile">
    <div class="k">{{ tile.label }}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ tile.value|fmt(tile.unit, 0) }}</div>
    <div class="meta">
      <span><a href="{{ tile.source_url }}">Pew Research Center</a></span>
      <span>companion · not in the BugOut Index</span>
    </div>
    <div class="age">{{ tile.question }}{% if tile.period %} · {{ tile.period }}{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="age">{{ tile.age_text }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% if pew_chart %}
<div class="chart-card">{{ pew_chart|safe }}</div>
<p class="chart-caption">Each point is a Pew survey date from the checklist excerpt, not a BugOut Index publication week. Not in the BugOut Index. Not the Edelman trust input.</p>
{% endif %}

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>Gallup confidence in institutions — shadow series</h3>
  <span class="hint">Not in the BugOut Index. No weight. “A great deal” plus “quite a lot.” Annual, typically June. Not the Edelman figure in the score.</span>
</div>
<p class="rev-callout">
  These readings are companions only. They are not in the BugOut Index and they have no weight.
  They are not interchangeable with the Edelman Trust Barometer US Government input.
  The checklist stores the current annual reading only. It is not a republication of Gallup’s historical series.
  Continuous republication of Gallup data may require permission.
  {% if gallup_reused_from %}
  This week’s checklist read failed; the values are carried forward from the {{ gallup_reused_from }} publish. The dates below are the survey dates in the checklist.
  {% endif %}
</p>
<div class="grid gallup">
  {% for tile in gallup_tiles %}
  <div class="tile">
    <div class="k">{{ tile.label }}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ tile.value|fmt(tile.unit, 0) }}</div>
    <div class="meta">
      <span><a href="{{ tile.source_url }}">Gallup</a></span>
      <span>companion · not in the BugOut Index</span>
    </div>
    <div class="age">{{ tile.question }}{% if tile.period %} · {{ tile.period }}{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="age">{{ tile.age_text }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% if gallup_chart %}
<div class="chart-card">{{ gallup_chart|safe }}</div>
<p class="chart-caption">Each point is a Gallup survey date from the checklist, not a BugOut Index publication week. Not in the BugOut Index.</p>
{% endif %}


<div class="section-title"><h3>About this index</h3></div>
<p style="max-width:70ch;color:var(--muted);">
  The BugOut Index is a directional stress and stability reading
  (methodology v{{ snapshot.methodology_version }}). Six published statistics sit between
  fixed endpoints and combine into one 0–100 score. Higher means those conditions are
  less stressed. The number shows how hard the published inputs are pressing. It is not
  a forecast, and it is not an instruction to bug out.
  Markets, the short-term pulse, labor utilization, food prices, the U.S. regional shelter companions, Pew public trust, and Gallup confidence in institutions on this page are companions.
  They are not in the score. Edelman remains the trust input. The shelter readings are local: New York City, Nashville–Davidson, Austin/Travis County, Ramsey County (Minnesota), Denver, and San Francisco. None of them is a U.S. total. Denver and San Francisco are occupancy rates, not headcounts. HUD AHAR remains the annual national homelessness input. Several inputs update monthly, quarterly, or once a year,
  so many weeks the number does not move.
  Crime under methodology 1.1.0 is the Real-Time Crime Index Nationwide Full Sample
  rate for the latest month in the file. Weeks through 2026-10-02 stay methodology
  1.0.0, with crime locked at 2,723.0.
  See <a href="./methodology.html">methodology</a> for the calculation, weights, and limits.
  The committed weekly files are the record of a past score. Rerunning the publisher
  fetches current observations and does not rebuild that week.
</p>
<p style="max-width:70ch;color:var(--muted);">
  For the long-horizon structural picture — whether the country is currently set up to
  produce broadly-shared prosperity and mobility over years and decades — see the
  <a href="https://adammontville.github.io/american-dream-reality-index/">American Dream Reality Index (ADRI)</a>.
  ADRI updates annually and weights toward education, health, real income, employment,
  inequality, and civic and safety fundamentals. The two indexes answer different
  questions. The BugOut Index is a weekly reading of pressure in a few published
  series. ADRI moves on slow structural conditions. Each can move for reasons the
  other does not catch.
</p>

{% endblock %}
